      "id": "23834282-9fa0-4155-be7a-c2f2228da39c",
      "name": "Cover Letter"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a job description parser.\n\nExtract structured information from the job posting HTML and return ONLY valid JSON.\n\nFields to extract:\n- job_title (string or null)\n- company_name (string or null)\n- required_skills (array of strings)\n- responsibilities (array of strings)\n- experience_required (string or null)\n- location (string or null)\n\nRules:\n1. Return ONLY JSON. No explanations, no markdown, no extra text.\n2. If a value is not clearly found, return null.\n3. required_skills and responsibilities must always be arrays (empty array if nothing found).\n4. Keep values short and clean. Do not copy large paragraphs.\n5. Extract only meaningful skills, not generic words like \"team player\" or \"communication\".\n\nExample output:\n\n{\n  \"job_title\": \"Frontend Developer\",\n  \"company_name\": \"PayPal\",\n  \"required_skills\": [\"JavaScript\", \"React\", \"HTML\", \"CSS\"],\n  \"responsibilities\": [\n    \"Build user interfaces\",\n    \"Collaborate with backend teams\",\n    \"Optimize performance\"\n  ],\n  \"experience_required\": \"2+ years\",\n  \"location\": \"Chennai, India\"\n}\n\nJob HTML:\n{{ $json.cleaned_html }}\n",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        -144,
